Key Functions of the Ultrasonic Sensor1. Obstacle Detection (Distance Measurement)Emits high-frequency sound waves ($40\text{ kHz}$) via a transmitter probe and listens for the echo returning to the receiver probe.  Calculates the precise distance to objects in front of the robot using the speed of sound.  2. Triggering Collision AvoidanceConstantly sends real-time distance values to the Arduino.  When an object comes within a set threshold (e.g., $25\text{ cm}$), it signals the microcontroller to halt or reverse the motors to prevent a physical crash.  3. Environment Mapping & Path PlanningWorks alongside motor logic to help the robot evaluate path clearance.  When mounted on a servo motor, it scans left and right to compare distance readings on both sides, allowing the robot to choose the path with the maximum clearance.4. Blind-Spot & Edge Detection (Application Dependent)Can be angled toward the floor or side walls to detect drops (like stairs or table edges) or to maintain a constant distance along a wall (wall-following capability).
